cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Fish: a benchmark for signalling under adversarial observation"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Fish benchmark contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/thetruthisntsweet/fish"
abstract: >-
  A rules engine, a PettingZoo multi-agent environment and baseline agents for the
  six-player team card game Fish, for measuring how much the way players act reveals
  about hidden information, how much they leak about their own hands, and whether any of
  it is deliberate signalling.
keywords:
  - card game
  - hidden information
  - multi-agent
  - reinforcement learning
  - benchmark
  - signalling
